<title>FRANCE: France will pay 80/75 pct of unpaid phone bills.</title>
<headline>France will pay 80/75 pct of unpaid phone bills.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government will pay 75 to 80 percent of an outstanding 2.5 billion franc debt in unpaid telephone bills, France Telecom chairman Michel Bon said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said the rest of the amount had been written off.</p>
<p>The unpaid bills go back to the period when France Telecom was a part of the state service.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue has been settled,&quot; Bon said, adding that the debt would be paid back over a short period and would carry interest.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
